  "term": "rubrospinal tract",
  "definition": "The rubrospinal tract is a long axon pathway in the spinal cord formed by fibers from neurons in the red nucleus. In this source, it is described as one of the motor projection tracts whose axons can be labeled to study injury and regeneration.",
